 ],
 "notes": "Street to the north, lake (Embalse Los Molinos) to the south. From the overhead drone view (two stone bedroom wings under shallow dark metal gables either side of a sunken courtyard, a central flat roof with the round skylight over the helical stair, the long living wing under the big dark gable, the pool beside it and the pale flat roof over the gallery), the oblique drone view, the lakeside elevations (glazed living floor with board-formed concrete ends over a stone lower floor with its own glass wall, raised pool on a stone plinth, steps down to a sunken lounge) and the entrance views (a curving steel-grating bridge with timber slat parapets crossing from street level to the door). The living wing is in fact turned a few degrees off the others; boxes can't rotate, so it is squared up. The bridge's curve is stepped. Slope simplified to a raised street strip; lower floors of the wings are shown full height. Dark-grey standing-seam roofs drawn as dark; pale gallery roof as metal."
}